{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" makes an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":") for your Mixpanel project in one call. It checks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the project token, posts to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/track","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" endpoint of the project’s data residency","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), with ","type":"text"},{"code":"verbose=1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", through a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", and splits each batch to Mixpanel’s limits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"): 2,000 events and 2 MB a request. A batch with no record the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It retries no response, a 5xx, 408","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and 429, waiting ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/mixpanel","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": Mixpanel’s recommended","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule, 2 s doubling to 60 s. The full jitter on top is Traffluent’s own choice. It drops and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reports any other status. The token goes in each event, so no header field is needed, and no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leaves this module out; import it on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The project token is public: Mixpanel’s own apps and web pages ship it. The destination takes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing else. Never put the project’s secret or a service account’s credentials in an app; they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"belong to Mixpanel’s import API, for servers. The factory throws "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":" for an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty token, and for one with a character other than a letter or digit, which no project token"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The region has no default. A project’s data resides in the US, the EU or India, and Mixpanel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ingests nothing for it from another residency’s endpoint, so you pick the region on purpose."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record becomes an event of an anonymous user. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the sessions enricher, also sent as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_id"},{"type":"text","text":"; a record with no session is sent under its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own record identifier, with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_id"},{"type":"text","text":". Under Simplified ID Merge, Mixpanel shows a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"session’s events under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device:<session>"},{"type":"text","text":", and a sessionless record’s under its bare record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier. No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$user_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$insert_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps, and its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":" the record’s timestamp in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"epoch milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent. Each event’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":", as is the endpoint’s, so Mixpanel adds no location from the request’s address. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"standard context is sent as Mixpanel’s default properties ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_version_string"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_build_number"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$model"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$wifi"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_version"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Mixpanel counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"text":", so each session is one user in its reports, and so is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each record sent without a session. On a Mixpanel plan billed by monthly tracked users, each counts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as one.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the encoder can’t write is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"starts with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":", as Mixpanel’s own events’ names do, one with a property Mixpanel reads for itself"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":"-prefixed one, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bucket"},{"type":"text","text":"), one of 255 properties or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"more counting the encoder’s own, one holding an array of 255 elements or more, one whose property"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nests objects more than 3 deep, one whose event isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp is before 1971 or has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"epoch-milliseconds form, and one too large for Mixpanel. The destination reports each as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel answers 200 even when it finds no valid event in a request. The endpoint asks for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verbose=1"},{"type":"text","text":", so the answer’s body says so, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{\"status\": 0, \"error\": ...}"},{"type":"text","text":", and the destination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drops the request and reports it as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.rejectedInBody(status:reason:recordIDs:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with Mixpanel’s error as the reason. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"status"},{"type":"text","text":" of 1 means only that one event or more was well"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"formed: it doesn’t confirm that the token names a project, so a wrong region, or a token of no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"project, may be answered 200 with nothing stored. Check the project’s Live View after setting the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination up. Its track API ingests only events from the last 5 days, so a record older than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that when it is sent isn’t stored, and is reported only when no event of its request was valid."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to PostHog or Amplitude, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AmplitudeEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import MixpanelEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let mixpanel = try HTTPDestination.mixpanel(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu or .india, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: mixpanel)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what Mixpanel receives, and why, in more detail."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"MixpanelEncoding"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"MixpanelEncoding","title":"MixpanelEncoding"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/mixpanel","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Mixpanel","title":"Sending to Mixpanel"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches","title":"Encoding batches"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out","title":"Records left out"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Mixpanel project through its track API."}],"references":{"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelEncodingError":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Why ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requests as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends nothing for the batch.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MixpanelEncodingError","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelEncodingError"}],"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelencodingerror"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives.","type":"text"}],"title":"HTTPDestinations"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/choosingdestinations":{"type":"link","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","title":"Choosing Destinations","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Choosing Destinations","type":"text"}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"BatchEncoder","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"What turns a batch of records into the requests ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" sends.","type":"text"}]},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelbatchencoder\/batchlimit","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"batchLimit"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","text":"BatchLimit"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Mixpanel’s limits on one request: 2,000 events, 2,000,000 bytes of body, and 999,999 bytes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of one event.","type":"text"}],"title":"batchLimit"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelSetupError":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError","title":"MixpanelSetupError","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"couldn’t make a destination."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelSetupError","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelSetupError","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelsetuperror"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelBatchEncoder":{"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelbatchencoder","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of Mixpanel’s track API, so an "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" can send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events to a Mixpanel project’s "},{"code":"POST \/track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MixpanelBatchEncoder"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends batches to the Mixpanel project of "},{"code":"projectToken","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", whose data"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resides in "},{"code":"region","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", through "},{"code":"transport","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the waits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of "},{"code":"backoff","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"code":"clock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Transport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPTransport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"kind":"symbol","title":"mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mixpanel","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"projectToken","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"region","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A6RegionO","text":"MixpanelRegion","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"plan","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","text":"TrackingPlan","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"transport","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"backoff","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clock","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","text":"Clock","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A10SetupErrorO","text":"MixpanelSetupError","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV","text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/mixpanel(projecttoken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/HTTPDestinations/ExponentialBackoff/mixpanel":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mixpanel","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV"}],"title":"mixpanel","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel’s recommended schedule, 2 s doubling to 60 s, with full jitter: a nominal wait of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"2 seconds before the first retry, doubling up to 60 seconds. Mixpanel recommends the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schedule; the full jitter is Traffluent’s, as for every destination."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/mixpanel","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/httpdestinations\/exponentialbackoff\/mixpanel","kind":"symbol"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Mixpanel project through its track API."}],"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","kind":"symbol","title":"MixpanelEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelRegion":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelRegion","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelRegion","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MixpanelRegion","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The data residency of a Mixpanel project, which decides the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/track"},{"type":"text","text":" endpoint its events are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"posted to."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelregion","kind":"symbol"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)":{"kind":"symbol","title":"mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"topic","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transport"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSessionTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encoding"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends batches to the Mixpanel project of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"projectToken"},{"type":"text","text":", whose data"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resides in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"region"},{"type":"text","text":", with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession.shared"},{"type":"text","text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"waits of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/mixpanel(projecttoken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mixpanel"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"projectToken"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"region"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A6RegionO","text":"MixpanelRegion"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","text":"TrackingPlan"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"backoff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","text":"ExponentialBackoff"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"clock"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","text":"Clock"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":">) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A10SetupErrorO","text":"MixpanelSetupError"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","text":"HTTPDestination"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations19URLSessionTransportV","text":"URLSessionTransport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV","text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]}}}